He led several projects, including the Intelligent Public Transportation Monitoring System in Johor, in collaboration with Pengangkutan Awam Johor (PAJ), a subsidiary of the Johor state government. The system was developed to replace the existing monitoring platform, providing real-time bus information, estimated arrival times, and operational reports for PAJ management.

He and his team also developed the IoT-based Data Collection and Analytics Framework using Bluetooth Proximity Beacons, a project funded by the National Institute of Information and Communications Technology (NICT), Japan. This project introduced an IoT-based solution to track bus locations and collect transportation data without relying on GPS, using Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) proximity beacons installed on buses and detection devices at bus stops. The system enables bus arrival detection, Estimated Time Arrival (ETA) computation, and data analytics through a cloud-based platform.

